At that time, Emil's age will be $E+5 = 19+5 = 24$.
Also, at that time, Emil's dad's age will be $D+5$, and Emil's brother's age will be $B+5$.

We are given that when Emil is 24, he will be half the age of his dad, so
$$ E+5 = \frac{1}{2}(D+5) $$
$$ 24 = \frac{1}{2}(D+5) $$
$$ 48 = D+5 $$
$$ D = 48 - 5 = 43 $$
We are also given that when Emil is 24, he will be twice as old as his brother, so
$$ E+5 = 2(B+5) $$
$$ 24 = 2(B+5) $$
$$ 12 = B+5 $$
$$ B = 12 - 5 = 7 $$
We want to find the sum of the ages of his dad and his brother now, which is $D+B$.
$$ D+B = 43 + 7 = 50 $$

